From d39cd1e5d325065217a9d9f3c966c7df2d3e8c6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sacha Gavino <sacha.gavino@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 11:11:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stage 4 Part 2: symbolic Jacobian sparsity (default),
 numerical retained

set_work_arrays rebuilt the Jacobian sparsity pattern on every solver step by
evaluating the Jacobian and keeping entries above 1e-99. That threshold is
value-dependent: it drops structurally-nonzero-but-tiny couplings, and which it
drops shifts step to step (docs/STAGE4_SPARSITY.md). Benign for pure gas-grain
chemistry -- the error test runs on the true RHS, so an incomplete Jacobian only
costs Newton iterations -- but a latent correctness bug for coagulation, where a
coupling that goes tiny as a bin empties (never disabled, just small) would drop
out of the pattern exactly when it matters. This replaces it, before coagulation
lands, with a fixed symbolic pattern built once from the reaction list.

New `sparsity` parameter: 'symbolic' (default) or 'numerical'.
  - symbolic: build_symbolic_sparsity() marks (row=any compound, col=any
    reactant) for every reaction, plus the diagonal -- a superset of every entry
    get_jacobian can ever write, with NO value-dependent pruning anywhere (the
    temperature-window / small-rate trap is thereby avoided by construction).
    Built once, reused every step.
  - numerical: the exact pre-stage-4 path, kept for reproducibility and pinned by
    the nmgc-2.0 equivalence test.

The pattern is assembled from an explicit list of (row, col) couplings, sorted
into CSC -- so coagulation can append its grain-column and cross-bin ice-transfer
couplings later without rewriting the builder.

A debug guard (sparsity_check_steps, default 5) asserts on the first N steps that
every numerically-nonzero Jacobian entry lies inside the symbolic pattern; by
construction it never fires -- if it ever does, the builder has a bug, not a
tolerance to relax. equivalence.sh now pins sparsity=numerical for the NEMO side
(same commit), so the external regression stays valid once symbolic is default.

Kept as its own commit: this is the one stage-4 change that could legitimately
alter the trajectory, so a later coagulation bisect can isolate it.

Verified:
  - numerical mode is byte-identical to the pre-Part-2 build (the refactor does
    not disturb the numerical path; the nmgc-2.0 equivalence is preserved);
  - the debug subset-assert held on every symbolic run;
  - gate (design-thread spec): per-species, evaluated as the max over output
    times, symbolic-vs-numerical difference must be <= the RTOL-perturbation
    difference for that same species, RTOL perturbed both ways (1e-4 -> 1.001e-4
    and 0.999e-4, max of the two). On the full-length reference run (1e5 yr, 20
    outputs, 911 species): the RTOL tweak moves species by up to 3.1e-3 relative,
    while symbolic-vs-numerical is exactly 0 -- symbolic is byte-identical to
    numerical here, not merely within the noise floor. Zero violations. Also
    byte-identical on a derived 4-bin MRN case, and tests/roundtrip_derived.sh
    passes under the (now default) symbolic path.

This closes Stage 4. The 0D gas-grain-dust skeleton is complete; coagulation is
the next stage.
